      "body": "## Overview\n\nLog the requested format, not the builtin `format`, when `endpoint-load-metrics-format` is unsupported.\n\n## Claims\n\n- The warning now names the unsupported format (for example `foo`) instead of `<built-in function format>`.\n\n## Validation\n\n`pytest tests/entrypoints/serve/utils/test_orca_metrics.py` (CPU, no GPU needed): the new test fails before (logged text contains `built-in function format`) and passes after.\n\n## Details\n\n`create_orca_header` passed `format` (the Python builtin) to the warning instead of `metrics_format`. One-word fix plus one unit test.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/vllm-project/codesmith/vllm/pr/63521?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28